            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> What should I do? Here is my mini.lua:\r\n\r\n'mini.files' doesn't support `:write` for updating disk to follow user edits. It has a dedicated [synchronize action](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/ddb70da6ec6aa896cfde87350d1e8dffb57ddef0/doc/mini-files.txt#L171) that is by default `=` key. So instead of `:write`, follow [the last two steps](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/ddb70da6ec6aa896cfde87350d1e8dffb57ddef0/doc/mini-files.txt#L236-L241) of how manipulation is expected to work.\r\n\r\nThe reasoning behind this decision is described in #391.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What should I do? Here is my mini.lua:</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">'mini.files' doesn't support <code class=\"notranslate\">:write</code> for updating disk to follow user edits. It has a dedicated <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/ddb70da6ec6aa896cfde87350d1e8dffb57ddef0/doc/mini-files.txt#L171\">synchronize action</a> that is by default <code class=\"notranslate\">=</code> key. So instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">:write</code>, follow <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/ddb70da6ec6aa896cfde87350d1e8dffb57ddef0/doc/mini-files.txt#L236-L241\">the last two steps</a> of how manipulation is expected to work.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The reasoning behind this decision is described in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1777368500\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/391\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/391/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/391\">#391</a>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "What should I do? Here is my mini.lua:\n\n'mini.files' doesn't support :write for updating disk to follow user edits. It has a dedicated synchronize action that is by default = key. So instead of :write, follow the last two steps of how manipulation is expected to work.\nThe reasoning behind this decision is described in #391.",
